Lab Tasks
Task 1: Viewing and Modifying Kernel Parameters with sysctl
Subtask 1.1: View Current Kernel Parameters
The sysctl command allows you to view and modify kernel parameters at runtime.

List all kernel parameters:

sudo sysctl -a
Expected Outcome: A long list of kernel parameters with their current values.
View a specific parameter (e.g., vm.swappiness):

sudo sysctl vm.swappiness
Expected Outcome: Displays the current value of vm.swappiness (e.g., vm.swappiness = 60).
Subtask 1.2: Modify a Kernel Parameter Temporarily
Changes made this way will not persist after a reboot.

Change vm.swappiness to a lower value (e.g., 10):

sudo sysctl -w vm.swappiness=10
Explanation: Lowering vm.swappiness reduces how aggressively the kernel swaps memory to disk.
Verify the change:

sudo sysctl vm.swappiness
Expected Outcome: Output should show vm.swappiness = 10.
Task 2: Tuning Network and Memory Management Settings
Subtask 2.1: Optimize Network Performance
Adjust TCP/IP stack parameters for better throughput.

Increase the maximum number of connections (e.g., net.core.somaxconn):

sudo sysctl -w net.core.somaxconn=1024
Explanation: This increases the backlog of pending connections.
Enable TCP Fast Open:

sudo sysctl -w net.ipv4.tcp_fastopen=3
Explanation: tcp_fastopen=3 enables Fast Open for both client and server.
Verify changes:

sudo sysctl net.core.somaxconn net.ipv4.tcp_fastopen
Expected Outcome: Displays updated values.
Subtask 2.2: Optimize Memory Management
Adjust virtual memory settings for better performance.

Reduce swap usage tendency (vm.swappiness):

sudo sysctl -w vm.swappiness=10
Increase file descriptor limits (fs.file-max):

sudo sysctl -w fs.file-max=2097152
Explanation: Increases the maximum number of open files.
Verify changes:

sudo sysctl vm.swappiness fs.file-max
Task 3: Persisting Kernel Changes Across Reboots
Subtask 3.1: Configure Persistent Kernel Parameters
To make changes permanent, modify /etc/sysctl.conf or create a new .conf in /etc/sysctl.d/.

Edit /etc/sysctl.conf:

sudo nano /etc/sysctl.conf
Add the following lines:

vm.swappiness = 10  
net.core.somaxconn = 1024  
net.ipv4.tcp_fastopen = 3  
fs.file-max = 2097152  
Apply changes without rebooting:

sudo sysctl -p
Expected Outcome: The changes are reloaded and applied.
Alternative: Use /etc/sysctl.d/ for modular configs:

sudo nano /etc/sysctl.d/99-custom.conf
Add the same parameters as above, then apply:

sudo sysctl --system
